  "worked_solution": "We are told that he buys $16$ liters of milk. The tape diagram for liters of milk shows $4$ boxes. Therefore, each box in the diagram above represents $16÷4=4$ liters.\n\nNow, we fill the number $4$ in each box of both tapes:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14187307/assets/c896618aebed4174005a7d47059eb74e24bc762645b8a46303a07e643c293407.png)\n\nSince there are $6$ boxes corresponding to the liters of juice and milk in total, and each box represents $4$ liters, the total number of liters is:\n\n$$\n4\\times 6=24\n$$\n\nSo, he buys $24$ liters of milk and juice altogether.",
